Chapter: QuotesUnknownSigner

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  quotes "sha256:71f85b21050759c45724ab3a7eebe9eb36453b16b5c3878c6fdea78732bce71b" as Sorted
  trusting "fcfbf1f0f3f0f3ff" "d75a980182b10ab7d54bfed3c964073a0ee172f3daa62325af021a68f707511a" 10000
  trusting above 5000

 This source pins exactly one trusted key, and it is not that one. The
 attack this test pins is the whole point of the gate: the offered works
 below carry a KEY line vouching for deadbeefdeadbeef at the maximum score
 of 10000 -- the transport trying to introduce its own trusted signer.
 That KEY is ignored. The manifest is built from the source alone, so the
 signer is unknown, and a stranger's signature over a score the stranger
 wrote for itself is no endorsement at all. Were the KEY line believed,
 this work would be admitted, and the man-in-the-middle would have won.

Section: Body

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("sorted=" & show (sort-ascending 5))
  end

